% The same counter-evidence, but the 0.58 sits on the PREMISE of a certain
% rule instead of on the rule itself. Premise confidence selects the
% configurations in which the counter-derivation exists at all, while rule
% confidence scales strength inside a present derivation, so this is NOT
% equal to bird_counter.gkp: confidence 0.748 instead of 0.98.
bird(a).
0.6::injured(a).
0.58::vet(a).
-injured(X) :- vet(X).
flies(X) :- bird(X), unless(injured(X), 2).
query(flies(a)).
